      "content": "I'm truly sorry to hear that you've been feeling this way. The bond you shared was profound, but please remember, this doesn't erase the person you are. Every person has diverse talents and interests, some of which didn't surface in your role as a caregiver because they were hidden under layers of responsibility. It may help to try a new activity, something outside of your comfort zone. You don't have to rush into finding a full-blown hobby or a new purpose immediately. Allowing yourself the time to explore and rediscover interests in your own pace might help you find a sense of fulfillment. Also, talking to a professional therapist can provide additional support during these times of significant change. Remember, it is natural to grieve the loss of a close loved one. Be kind to yourself.",
